# SHA-256 of identifiers that must never appear in this repository.
#
# Hashes, not terms, and deliberately so: a file listing what you are hiding is
# itself the disclosure, and this repository is public. Nobody — including the
# guard — can read the vocabulary back out of this file.
#
# Add one with:  node tools/identifier-guard.mjs --add <term>
# That writes the digest and never the term, not even to your shell history if
# you prefix the command with a space.
#
# Terms are normalised before hashing: lowercased, with commas, whitespace and
# leading/trailing dots and slashes removed. So a path prefix is caught inside a
# longer path, and a formatted number is caught however it is punctuated.
